  "goodToKnow": "Der Gerichtshof is a court, used for high and international courts: der Bundesgerichtshof (BGH, Germany's highest court for civil and criminal law, in Karlsruhe), der Europäische Gerichtshof (EuGH, in Luxembourg), der Internationale Strafgerichtshof (in The Hague). Ordinary courts are simply das Gericht. Karlsruhe also hosts the Bundesverfassungsgericht, so Karlsruhe has entschieden often means a top court has ruled."
